    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is primed for a high-output performance today, led by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (78.30) and **Will Smith** (74.85). **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains our most consistent engine, benefiting from an elite combination of base skill and a favorable matchup against Abbott. Meanwhile, **Will Smith** draws a prime opportunity against Kochanowicz (5.19 xERA), where his xwOBA profile and advantageous batting order slot make him a must-start. **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (72.67) also provide significant ceiling potential today; **Lawrence Butler** leverages a substantial platoon edge (13%) against Mahle, while **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a strong park factor and a clean look at the Freeland matchup, reinforcing our strategy of chasing high-efficiency, speed-adjacent profiles to close the gap in our scarcest category.\n\nThe decision to bench **Masyn Winn** (53.15) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Masyn Winn** offers the stolen base upside we prioritize, he is suppressed today by an Elite Hold SP profile from Wacha, which negatively impacts his efficiency relative to the rest of the infield. Ultimately, we opted for the higher floor provided by **Jeremiah Jackson**, despite the latter facing a tough catcher efficiency hurdle. We are closely monitoring the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains inactive on the IL; his absence necessitates disciplined management of our game caps. **Brendan Donovan** (66.36) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65) round out the lineup as strong plays against Civale and V\u00e1squez, respectively, with both hitters effectively utilizing the positive park and platoon adjustments baked into our daily projections. Keep an eye on any late-inning weather alerts, though currently, the primary risk to our production remains the league-leading defense of opposing catchers curbing our stolen base attempts.",
